* A kind=sig2phys converter has no terminals and stamps nothing into the MNA system -- it is
* consumed by *name* (an independent source's own value field, or an ideal switch's
* gate=/ctrl=), never by a wire. Here R1 wires node "VDRV", which merely happens to be the
* converter's name, so nothing drives that node at all: `G*v = 0` is perfectly non-singular and
* the run used to succeed silently, reporting V(VDRV) = 0 next to the block's own correct,
* non-zero VDRV output column. It must be a hard build-time error instead
* (DaeError::Sig2PhysUsedAsCircuitNode), in --mode dc as well as --mode transient.
CMD kind=const value=5
VDRV kind=sig2phys domain=voltage in=CMD
R1 VDRV 0 1k
